FlClash core wrapper
Source: https://github.com/chen08209/FlClash
Revision: 7fd417fb9a9a277c6a9339a8ac87f907df7c25f7
License: GNU GPL v3 (see LICENSE and licenses/FlClash-LICENSE)
The Go wrapper is used to build the Android bridge and the desktop core process.
Change by Rooni, 2026-11-01: core/dial_pipe.go also accepts a loopback TCP
port for IPC on Windows. The replacement is in scripts/core-patches/.
Change by Rooni, 2026-11-02: mihomo component/tls/reality.go reports client
version 26.10.31 instead of 1.8.2 in the REALITY handshake, so servers with
minClientVer accept it. Applied by scripts/core-patches/reality-version.sh.
The Kotlin UI and application logic are developed separately in this project.

